{"parentUuid":"5fab8196-564b-4917-a1d7-68accdf0bcca","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"f74dfbbe-e023-4225-96f3-eaf795cf8ebf","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EpL2vQ6KZPmhQyQ8Srsyww","type":"tool_result","content":"44\t    if (!farmerId) { router.replace('/farmer/login'); return }\n45\t\n46\t    setLoading(true)\n47\t    // Explicit columns: handover_otp is deliberately NOT fetched — the pickup\n48\t    // code must come from the customer, so the farmer's browser never sees it.\n49\t    const { data } = await supabase\n50\t      .from('orders')\n51\t      .select('id, farmer_id, order_code, produce_listing_id, produce_name, quantity, unit, total_price, buyer_name, buyer_phone, pickup_location, status, payment_status, decline_reason, refund_status, refund_amount, refunded_at, delivery_type, collected_at, fulfillment_date, created_at')\n52\t      .eq('farmer_id', farmerId)\n53\t      .in('status', ['approved', 'declined'])\n54\t      .order('created_at', { ascending: false })\n55\t\n56\t    setOrders((data ?? []) as Order[])\n57\t    setLoading(false)\n58\t  }, [router])\n59\t\n60\t  useEffect(() => { load() }, [load])\n61\t\n62\t  // Farmer sets/updates the pickup-or-delivery date on an approved order.\n63\t  const setFulfillmentDate = async (orderId: string, date: string) => {\n64\t    const value = date || null\n65\t    setOrders((prev) => prev.map((o) => (o.id === orderId ? { ...o, fulfillment_date: value } : o)))\n66\t    await supabase.from('orders').update({ fulfillment_date: value }).eq('id', orderId)\n67\t  }\n68\t\n69\t  const filterStart = () => {\n70\t    if (filter === 'today') {\n71\t      const d = new Date()\n72\t      d.setHours(0, 0, 0, 0)\n73\t      return d.getTime()"}]},"uuid":"8b1f239f-8957-455d-b52c-36f3b6a772b9","timestamp":"2026-06-16T18:46:15.548Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/veerendra/farmer/yourfamilyfarmer/src/app/farmer/dashboard/orders/page.tsx","content":"    if (!farmerId) { router.replace('/farmer/login'); return }\n\n    setLoading(true)\n    // Explicit columns: handover_otp is deliberately NOT fetched — the pickup\n    // code must come from the customer, so the farmer's browser never sees it.\n    const { data } = await supabase\n      .from('orders')\n      .select('id, farmer_id, order_code, produce_listing_id, produce_name, quantity, unit, total_price, buyer_name, buyer_phone, pickup_location, status, payment_status, decline_reason, refund_status, refund_amount, refunded_at, delivery_type, collected_at, fulfillment_date, created_at')\n      .eq('farmer_id', farmerId)\n      .in('status', ['approved', 'declined'])\n      .order('created_at', { ascending: false })\n\n    setOrders((data ?? []) as Order[])\n    setLoading(false)\n  }, [router])\n\n  useEffect(() => { load() }, [load])\n\n  // Farmer sets/updates the pickup-or-delivery date on an approved order.\n  const setFulfillmentDate = async (orderId: string, date: string) => {\n    const value = date || null\n    setOrders((prev) => prev.map((o) => (o.id === orderId ? { ...o, fulfillment_date: value } : o)))\n    await supabase.from('orders').update({ fulfillment_date: value }).eq('id', orderId)\n  }\n\n  const filterStart = () => {\n    if (filter === 'today') {\n      const d = new Date()\n      d.setHours(0, 0, 0, 0)\n      return d.getTime()","numLines":30,"startLine":44,"totalLines":252}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5fab8196-564b-4917-a1d7-68accdf0bcca","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/veerendra/farmer/yourfamilyfarmer","sessionId":"a9aae61b-4a55-4f27-b7c0-22d7e61b6fa7","version":"2.1.178","gitBranch":"feat/suspend-consumer-reason-privacy"}
{"parentUuid":"8b1f239f-8957-455d-b52c-36f3b6a772b9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Yc2r28kSShy4MpZGktvnKF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Investigated thoroughly. Short answer: **this is essentially not built yet** — it's a net-new feature. Only adjacent scaffolding exists, and there's one design conflict you'll need to resolve. Here's the breakdown:\n\n## What's missing (the core of this request)\n\n| Piece | Status |\n|---|---|\n| DB columns `shipped_at`, `received_at` | ❌ Don't exist anywhere |\n| `'shipped'` / `'completed'` order status | ❌ Don't exist (orders only use `pending`/`approved`/`declined`) |\n| Farmer \"Picked Up / తీసుకువెళ్ళారు\" button | ❌ Not in dashboard |\n| Farmer \"Shipped / షిప్ చేయబడింది\" button | ❌ Not in dashboard |\n| Consumer \"Received / అందుకున్నాను\" button | ❌ Not on consumer order page |\n| API routes (mark shipped / received / picked-up) | ❌ None exist |\n| Status-change notifications (farmer + consumer) | ❌ No notification infra at all (only `moderator/notify-scarce`; Twilio not wired) |\n\n## What partially exists (related, but not this)\n\n- **`picked_up_at` already exists** — but it belongs to the **rider/delivery-boy flow**, not a farmer \"Picked Up\" button. Don't reuse it for this.\n- **`collected_at` + a `confirm-pickup` API route exist** for self-pickup — but it's an **OTP-based** confirmation (buyer gives farmer a code), and it's **not wired to any UI button**. Your request wants a simple one-tap \"Picked Up\" with no OTP.\n- The **uncommitted dashboard work** already moves resolved orders out of the active list (pickup → `collected_at` set; home_delivery → `delivery_status='delivered'`), so the \"active vs history\" plumbing partly exists.\n- The **consumer order timeline exists** (`consumer/orders/[id]/page.tsx`) and shows dates for placed/paid/picked-up — but has **no Shipped or Received steps**.\n- The \"Order History\" page (`farmer/dashboard/orders/page.tsx`) just lists `approved`+`declined` orders — there's no `completed` concept.\n\n## ⚠️ One conflict you need to decide before I build\n\nYour request models **courier as farmer-managed** (farmer taps Shipped → consumer taps Received). But the codebase already has a **rider-managed `home_delivery` flow** with its own statuses (`assigned → picked_up → out_for_delivery → delivered`), OTP handover, and an admin rider-assignment screen. There's also a separate `'courier'` `delivery_type` value floating around.\n\nSo \"courier/shipped\" could mean either:\n- **(A)** A new *self-ship* path (farmer posts a parcel themselves, no rider) — fully separate from the existing rider flow, OR\n- **(B)** A rename/repurpose of the existing rider `home_delivery` flow.\n\nThis changes the whole implementation. Let me confirm before writing code."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01V4ZXfwQNMrz8q4YGLEJVUJ","name":"AskUserQuestion","input":{"questions":[{"question":"You want this order-completion flow built — how should the 'courier/shipped' path relate to the existing rider delivery flow?","header":"Courier model","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"New self-ship path","description":"Courier = farmer ships the parcel themselves (post/courier service), no rider involved. Farmer taps Shipped, consumer taps Received. Existing rider home_delivery flow stays untouched as a separate option."},{"label":"Repurpose rider flow","description":"The existing rider home_delivery flow IS the courier flow. Map Shipped/Received onto it (and drop or hide the rider/delivery-boy steps)."},{"label":"Just tell me the gaps","description":"Don't build yet — you only wanted the status assessment above, not implementation right now."}]},{"question":"For the farmer's 'Picked Up' button on pickup orders, which behavior do you want?","header":"Pickup confirm","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"Simple one-tap","description":"Farmer just taps