{"parentUuid":"d71cf1fc-988e-4e35-bd42-911b276ae113","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01SCve7vjykRykeogwyTM6qy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I loaded the plan tool but I'm not actually in plan mode, so I'll lay the plan out here. This touches the buyer-facing checkout, the DB, and several pages, so I want your green light before I start.\n\n## Plan: order completion flow (pickup + courier self-ship)\n\n**The catch:** today every delivery order is `home_delivery` = the rider flow. There is no \"farmer ships it themselves\" order type. Since you chose a *new* self-ship path with the rider flow untouched, I have to introduce a real `courier` order type, which means a small checkout change too.\n\n### 1. DB migration (`scripts/order-completion-migration.sql` + apply via Supabase)\nAdd to `orders`:\n- `shipped_at timestamptz` — farmer marked courier parcel shipped\n- `received_at timestamptz` — consumer confirmed receipt\n- *(skip a new `picked_up_at`)* — pickup completion reuses the existing `collected_at` column, which already means exactly \"collected\" and is already wired into the active/history split. Adding a third pickup column would create two sources of truth. I'll flag this deviation from your column list — tell me if you'd rather I add `picked_up_at` literally.\n\n### 2. Checkout (`Cart.tsx` + `api/orders/place`)\n- When the farmer's mode is `courier`/`both`, offer a **\"Courier / షిప్పింగ్\"** delivery option alongside self-pickup (distinct from the rider \"Home delivery\").\n- `place` route accepts and stores `delivery_type='courier'`.\n\n### 3. Farmer dashboard (`farmer/dashboard/page.tsx`)\n- On an **approved `self_pickup`** order: **\"✓ Picked Up / తీసుకువెళ్ళారు\"** button → one-tap, sets `collected_at` → order leaves Active Orders.\n- On an **approved `courier`** order: **\"📦 Shipped / షిప్ చేయబడింది\"** button → sets `shipped_at`, stays in Active Orders showing \"Shipped — awaiting receipt\".\n- `isResolved()` updated: pickup→`collected_at`; courier→`received_at`; home_delivery→rider `delivered` (unchanged).\n\n### 4. New API routes\n- `POST /api/farmer/orders/[id]/picked-up` → sets `collected_at`\n- `POST /api/farmer/orders/[id]/ship` → sets `shipped_at`\n- `POST /api/consumer/orders/[id]/received` → sets `received_at`\n\n### 5. Consumer order page (`consumer/orders/[id]/page.tsx`)\n- On a shipped courier order: **\"✓ Received / అందుకున్నాను\"** button → sets `received_at` → moves to history.\n- Add **Shipped** and **Received** steps (with dates) to the timeline; add a pickup \"Picked up\" date. Add lightweight polling so the buyer sees \"Shipped\" without a manual refresh.\n\n### 6. Notifications\nThere is **no push/WhatsApp infra** (Twilio is unbuilt — P3). So \"notifications\" = **in-app**: the farmer dashboard already live-updates via Supabase realtime (sees \"Received\" automatically); I'll add polling on the consumer page so they see \"Shipped\". A real WhatsApp/push notification is out of scope unless you want me to wire Twilio (separate effort).\n\n### 7. Translations\nAll new labels in `translations.ts` (en + te).\n\n---\n\n**Two things to confirm:**\n1. OK to add the **courier checkout option** (small buyer-facing change)? Without it, no order can ever *be* a courier order.\n2. OK to **reuse `collected_at`** for pickup instead of adding a literal `picked_up_at` column?\n\nReply and I'll build it."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":65561,"cache_read_input_tokens":8198,"output_tokens":1792,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":65561,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1792,"cache_read_input_tokens":8198,"cache_creation_input_tokens":65561,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5